    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1957" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">allŏphȳ^lus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλλόφυλος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of another stock</i> or <i>race</i>,
				<i>foreign</i> (the orig. long <i>y</i> is shortened in the poets): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenuerunt eum allophyli,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Psa. 55, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjugium allophylorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pud. 7</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. ad Eust. 27 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tyrannus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 502</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Paul. Nol. de S. Fel. Nat. Carm. 8,
				23, 70</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4,
			37</span></i>.</div>
